export anchor RecipeCardStyle:
    number: 80
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Recipe card
    idea: Every project is a handwritten index recipe card on a gingham-bordered counter, with tasks measured in cups, a jug that fills as work is done and a stamp for the status.
    base: light
    palette:
        gingham: #c94141, the checked border at 55 percent on white
        counter: #fbf6ea, the page inside the border
        card: #fffdf6, index cards
        topRule: #d0453f, the red line under card titles
        ruledBlue: #a9cbe8, card lines, decoration only
        pencil: #26262f, writing and outlines
        faded: #57525c, typed field labels
        butter: #f8e7b0, jug fill and the notification badge
        tomato: #ac2727, the primary button, Behind, the overdue line and this week bars
        herb: #2e6a30, the On track stamp
        honey: #875700, the At risk stamp
        blueInk: #1f4e9a, links, jug marks and focus
    type:
        Handwriting uses Segoe Print, Bradley Hand, Chalkboard SE, Comic
        Sans MS, Comic Neue, cursive for the brand at 34px, the greeting at
        30px, card titles at 21px on a 38px line and card lines at 16px on a
        26px rule. Typed field labels use Courier New, Courier at 11px bold
        caps. Body notes use Trebuchet MS, Gill Sans, Segoe UI at 13 to
        15px.
    layout:
        The whole page sits inside a red gingham border with a white and red
        double edge. The header has a basket mark with Brightwork in tomato
        script and THE TEAM RECIPE BOX in type, a hand-cut search, a tomato
        New project button, a round timer bell with a butter 3 badge and
        Head cook Mara Okafor. Nav is a row of recipe-box divider tabs with
        Home raised in front. The greeting card says Good morning, Mara,
        the date, a tomato line that 4 tasks are overdue and to check the
        oven first, and that everything else is simmering. Beside it an In
        the pantry card lists the four summary numbers with a cup, spoon,
        timer and sand glass. Recipes on the go is a grid of six tilted
        cards, each with a ruled body, a red title rule, the title with a
        status stamp, typed fields From, Measured as tasks in cups, Done and
        Ready by, a jug drawing filled to the percent and a one-line method.
        Below sit Batches baked, a bar chart with open rounded bars last
        week and tomato bars this week, and Kitchen notes on a ruled card.
        At 375px the border thins and cards stack.
    spacing: Set by the 26px ruled line. 22px between cards and 18px card padding.
    density: Medium. Four facts per card plus a jug.
    corners: 3px card corners. Buttons and fields use uneven hand-cut corners such as 4px 16px.
    borders: The gingham frame round the page, a 2px red title rule and blue lines on cards, and 2px pencil outlines on controls.
    shadows: A soft paper shadow under cards and a 2px by 3px pencil offset under buttons. Cards tilt under one degree.
    icons:
        Kitchen line drawings, a jug, a spoon, a timer and a sand glass.
        Stamps are rotated outlined boxes pairing the word with a ticked
        circle for On track, a triangle for At risk and a crossed solid
        square for Behind.
    focus: A 3px dashed blue ink outline offset 3px.
    tone: Warm and homely, such as Heads up, check the oven first, Recipes on the go, Kitchen notes and Ready by.
